course: dictionary
lesson: 14910
title: Redecorate and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To redecorate a room is to make it look new again. You might paint the walls, put up new wallpaper, or change the curtains and furniture. «We will redecorate the bedroom in blue.» The word starts with re, which often means again, and decorate means to make something look nice.
explain: «Mum wants to redecorate the kitchen next summer.» The clue is the time: next summer, so she is planning a change, not a mess. Always check the clues around the word to find its meaning.
explain: Redecorate can also be a joke. «The toddler has redecorated the hallway with jam!» Is the hallway tidier or messier? Messier, so this means a big mess, not a nice change.
explain: In maths, redecorating can be a problem about area. «The bedroom walls have an area of 24 square metres.» To find out how much paint you need to redecorate, you use the area, then work out how many tins to buy and what they cost.
fact: To redecorate means to make a room or house look new again.
fact: Redecorate is a verb: redecorate, redecorates, redecorated, redecorating.
fact: «Redecorated» shows that the change has already happened, in the past.
fact: The joking meaning: a toddler who spreads food on the walls has «redecorated» the room, but it is a mess, not an improvement.
fact: Phrases such as «redecorate in blue» mean to decorate again using blue paint or colour.
exercise: «Families often redecorate their bedrooms.» What does redecorate mean? | Clean the floor only | Move to a new house | *Make a room look new again | Make a room very dark
exercise: «The toddler redecorated the kitchen with yoghurt.» Is this a nice change or a joke about a mess? | A kitchen that is wet from rain | *A joke about a big mess | A kitchen with new curtains | A new, tidy kitchen
exercise: The walls need paint. Why would you measure their area? | To count the chairs | *To work out how much paint is needed | To decide the name of the room | To find out the colour of the walls
test: «Classrooms get redecorated in the holidays.» What does the ending -ed show in redecorated? | It is a noun for a room | *It happened in the past | It will happen in the future | It is happening right now
test: The wallpaper is old and faded. Which word means to make the room look new again? | *redecorate | sleep | tidy the desk | measure
exam: «We will redecorate the bedroom in green, and the paint costs £20 a tin.» What does redecorate mean here? | To break the bedroom door | To count the tins of paint | *To make the bedroom look new again with paint | To make a big mess on the walls
